dan normal form) of $A,$ and $P$ is an invertible matrix.\n\nTo find the matrix $J,$ we first find the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ by solving $det(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-10-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 8 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda )-(-2)\\cdot 8 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+12\\lambda +36 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +6)(\\lambda +6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=-6.$ \n\nSince $A$ is not a scalar matrix, we conclude that $A$ is not diagonalizable, and its Jordan canonical form is\n\n$$\nJ={J}_{2}(-6)=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9d46200f-1674-5061-b28b-bbacea4c478e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9d46200f-1674-5061-b28b-bbacea4c478e" :answer-field/id #uuid "9d46200f-1674-5061-b28b-bbacea4c478e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2997e2ff-2037-5552-b0bd-698795cf62e4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dda58d8b-c65f-5bb6-910b-6e1345e0dd12" "answer-a1e158f2-e157-5bef-b2f6-497683140d4c" "answer-0ef2032d-530d-50c1-908e-9d91e9d7cad4" "answer-2997e2ff-2037-5552-b0bd-698795cf62e4" "answer-1fe7266d-5234-5afc-ad8b-4d38abe1dc8f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dda58d8b-c65f-5bb6-910b-6e1345e0dd12" :answer/id #uuid "dda58d8b-c65f-5bb6-910b-6e1345e0dd12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1e158f2-e157-5bef-b2f6-497683140d4c" :answer/id #uuid "a1e158f2-e157-5bef-b2f6-497683140d4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ef2032d-530d-50c1-908e-9d91e9d7cad4" :answer/id #uuid "0ef2032d-530d-50c1-908e-9d91e9d7cad4" :answer/type :